%N A337367 Sum of squared end-to-end distances over all n-step self-avoiding walks on the square lattice having no pair of nonconsecutive vertices that are adjacent in the lattice.
%C A337367 The corresponding number of n-step walks is given in A173380.
%C A337367 From _Carlo Corti_, Aug 14 2026: (Start)
%C A337367 Previous name was: Sum of square end-to-end distance over all self-avoiding n-step walks on a square lattice where no adjacent points are allowed, except those for consecutive steps.
%C A337367 The rows with contact number m = 0 in the ancillary file sq_isaw_EE.ser accompanying Beaton, Guttmann, and Jensen (2020) give a(n) for 2 <= n <= 45. (End)
%D A337367 N. J. A. Sloane and Simon Plouffe, The Encyclopedia of Integer Sequences, Academic Press, 1995 (includes the sequence A173380).
%H A337367 Carlo Corti, <a href="/A337367/b337367.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..45</a>
%H A337367 N. R. Beaton, A. J. Guttmann, and I. Jensen, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1911.05852">Two-dimensional interacting self-avoiding walks: new estimates for critical temperatures and exponents</a>, arXiv:1911.05852 [cond-mat.stat-mech], 2020. See ancillary file sq_isaw_EE.ser.
%H A337367 Sequence Fans Mailing list, <a href="https://web.archive.org/web/*/http://list.seqfan.eu/oldermail/seqfan/2010-November/006470.html">discussion of the sequence A173380</a>, November 2010.
%F A337367 Let E_n(u) = Sum_{omega in Omega_n} |omega_0 - omega_n|^2*u^(c(omega)), where Omega_n is the set of n-step self-avoiding walks on the square lattice and c(omega) is the number of pairs of nonconsecutive vertices that are adjacent in the lattice. Then a(n) = [u^0] E_n(u). - _Carlo Corti_, Aug 14 2026
%e A337367 The allowed 4-step walks with their associated end-to-end square distances are:
%e A337367 .
%e A337367          + 10
%e A337367 4        |        8              8      8           16
%e A337367 +--+     +     +--+              +      +    X--+---+---+---+
%e A337367    |     |     |          10     |      |
%e A337367    +     +     +     +--+--+  +--+      +        +--+ 10      + 10
%e A337367    |     |     |     |        |         |        |            |
%e A337367 X--+  X--+  X--+  X--+     X--+   X--+--+  X--+--+   X--+--+--+
%e A337367 .
%e A337367 The eight non-straight walks sum to 68, and these can be walked in eight ways on the square lattice. The remaining straight walk can be walking in four ways. Thus a(4) = 68 * 8 + 16 * 4 = 608.
%Y A337367 Cf. A173380 (corresponding number of walks), A336448 (sum of squared end-to-end distances over all square-lattice self-avoiding walks), A001411 (corresponding number of all square-lattice self-avoiding walks).
%K A337367 nonn,walk,changed
%O A337367 0,2
%A A337367 _Scott R. Shannon_, Aug 25 2020
%E A337367 Name edited and a(29)-a(31) from _Carlo Corti_, Aug 14 2026
